lead:
  - "Think of a family as one of those mobiles that hang over a crib. Every piece is tied to every other piece, so when one part gets pulled, the whole thing swings, even the parts that were holding perfectly still. That's why the person who ends up in the most pain often isn't the source of the trouble. They're just the piece the tension is tugging on hardest."
  - "So what happens when you try to fix a mobile by grabbing only the one swinging piece? It thrashes harder. Family therapy works differently. Instead of hunting for the person to blame, we watch how the whole thing moves together, and we help the family find a new balance that doesn't cost any one member their peace. Whose fault is it? Almost always the wrong question."
